{
  "title": "GR00T N1: An Open Foundation Model for Generalist Humanoid Robots",
  "authors": [
    "NVIDIA"
  ],
  "year": 2025,
  "arxivId": "2503.14734",
  "abstract": "GR00T N1 is a foundation model for generalist humanoid robots, trained on a diverse set of data sources to enable robots to reason about novel situations and learn new tasks rapidly. The model uses a dual-system architecture, consisting of a vision-language module and a diffusion transformer module, to generate fluid motor actions in real-time.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "GR00T N1 is a <strong>Vision-Language-Action (VLA) model</strong> that generates actions from image and language instruction input. It has <strong>cross-embodiment support</strong> from tabletop robot arms to dexterous humanoid robots. The model uses a <strong>dual-system compositional architecture</strong>, inspired by human cognitive processing.",
